            <div xml:id="d715">

                <pb facs="0786" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.51/1282: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-06-23T19:00:00-04:00">June 23, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Please report by telegraph whether you have conveyed to President Benavides
                    the substance of the Department’s telegram no. 39, June 13, 1 p.m. and whether
                    he understands that there must be a most careful and thorough preliminary
                    exploration of the possibilities before a Peruvian mission is sent to
                    Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
